{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/310448-silver-madness-and-antagonists-in-armor","id":310448,"title":"Silver, Madness, and Antagonists in Armor","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-12T12:37:30-08:00","id":310448,"title":"Silver, Madness, and Antagonists in Armor","content":"I saw this armor one day when reading about a Japanese show from the creator of Power Rangers on Wikipedia. The reasons why I came across it aren't important so much as the idea that suddenly struck me upon seeing it.<br /> <br /> What kind of horror would possess an Uratha to don silver armor? Surely only an insane one might do it. Or maybe was made to do it? I started to ponder. I wanted to formulate a legend and a brutal antagonist.<br /> <br /> ...but I'm not very familiar with Werewolf. My group is waiting for Second Edition before diving in. I've read a few First Edition books and the core, but I wanted to ask the community, are there any hooks already out there, reasons for a Werewolf's soul, mind or body to be trapped in silver armor? Are there any legends already out there for me to start from or should I cloth this whole from something entirely new?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://img2.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20120425004132/garo/images/a/a6/BaragoEp1922-24.png\" target=\"_blank\">http://img2.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb2...oEp1922-24.png</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://4.bp.blogspot.com/-GEDk3E2K2Yo/T6_n8vPbrFI/AAAAAAAADaA/rjjZ6Xei26k/s1600/Garo+Zero.png\" target=\"_blank\">http://4.bp.blogspot.com/-GEDk3E2K2Y.../Garo+Zero.png</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T13:49:45-08:00","id":310517,"title":"","content":"Looks like the Rite of the Final Moonrise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T14:00:40-08:00","id":310527,"title":"","content":"Sounds like something an Ivory Claw would get up to. They're pretty big on self torture just to show how tough they are. That and their totem is Silver Wolf, so I could totally see an antagonist who either wears silver armor blessed by his totem, or who bound his soul to a silver suit of armor to better serve the totem. Sounds like some cool stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T14:28:36-08:00","id":310565,"title":"","content":"Pick a human being host to a spirit with Wolf-Slayer gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T04:44:49-08:00","id":311115,"title":"","content":"The main problem with this (unless the armor was magical at its core, i.e. the protection was magical) is that silver is super weak. It'd be useless as armor compared to other, more reliable materials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T12:32:26-08:00","id":311514,"title":"","content":"Silver plated then so it is strong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T13:03:29-08:00","id":311575,"title":"","content":"Does it have to be silver armor per se? Because I may have something that would interest you, only... it's not exactly armor.<br /> <br /> If interested, I'll be more than happy to post again when I get home.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It's a rite similar to the Rite of the Final Moonrise. If you're fine with something like that, I'll happily post mine here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3702,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","user":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","date":". 11-13-2014, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T16:22:11-08:00","id":311717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ursufgutha Storm-Born</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/310448-silver-madness-and-antagonists-in-armor?p=311575#post311575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it have to be silver armor per se? Because I may have something that would interest you, only... it's not exactly armor.<br /> <br /> If interested, I'll be more than happy to post again when I get home.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It's a rite similar to the Rite of the Final Moonrise. If you're fine with something like that, I'll happily post mine here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure I'm open to any idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T17:03:37-08:00","id":314043,"title":"","content":"Maybe a Forsaken or Pure who's gone mad, convinced that the very existence of Werewolves causes the trouble with spirits, and is running around using Fetish armor and Gifts to wipe his kin of the face of the earth, Othar style?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T09:08:53-08:00","id":314586,"title":"","content":"Sorry this took a while GilboD; swamped with work, then family and RL friends and other responsibilities. But, as promised, here's my offering to your idea pool. I hope you like it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Tank could not believe what was happening to him. The Pure had caught him, broken his body and stolen his Rage, and then hauled him in chains to their hallowed grounds. What awaited him there\u2026 was a goddamned rally, almost twenty wolves strong. Had they been there all this time? he numbly wondered as they unceremoniously rolled him atop a flattened slab of stone \u2013 an altar.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, silence swept across the clearing, and the swarthy skinned </i>Rahu <i>heard footsteps approaching. \u201cBrothers!\u201d cried a man\u2019s voice, melodious yet stentorian, \u201cSisters! Tonight you stand in the presence of our gods, Lords </i>Hathis<i>, </i>Huzuruth<i>, and </i>Gurim!<i> Tonight you bear witness as they judge this Moon-loved, Forsaken, </i>motherfucker!\u201d<i> the speaker growls, punctuating the last word with a blow to the back of the captive\u2019s head and eliciting a cheer from the gathered </i>Anshega<i>. Tank groaned, thoughts swimming from the pain. Nonetheless he heard as the footsteps moved away from the altar, the speaker pausing for the clamor to die down before he continued.<br /> <br /> \u201cWould that he should repent of the Mother and her traitorous ways,\u201d the speech resumed, more solemnly this time. \u201cWould that he should turn around and embrace Father Wolf! But in his heart, he has stricken </i>Urfarah <i>dead, clinging to the love of the Moon-Bitch so; for why should he, unless he believed that </i>Urfarah <i>dead cannot judge him for his betrayal?\u201d<br /> <br /> A hush had fallen over the </i>Uratha <i>crowd then, seething with tension. Tank shuddered as he caught a whiff of them, boiling with barely restrained Rage. With </i>hate<i>.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlas,\u201d said the speaker softly, \u201cUntil the day we bring </i>Taga Dan <i>upon this cursed earth and Father Wolf rejoins us, it falls to his Pure children - us - to punish the Enemy in his stead. Let judgment now then be pronounced by no less than </i>Urfarah\u2019s<i> most faithful Firstborn sons! Apostle Maul, Brother Carver, come forth!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat the fuck are you doing to me? The FUCK are you doing to me?!\u201d screamed Tank, growling and trembling furiously as he tried to shake off his iron bonds. Soon there were three </i>Anshega <i>standing around the altar, laying clawed, calloused </i>Dalu <i>hands upon him, chanting in darkly intoned </i>Uremehir<i>:</i><br /> <br /> &lt;Lord Huzuruth, Lord Hathis, and Lord Gurim, we beseech thee to hear our prayer. So long have the Urdaga of this place suckled at the Moon-Bitch\u2019s teat, forgetting our Father and turning their backs to his Truth. So speak we retribution, beginning with this one; we invoke the Rite of Purgation, of fury, fire, and argent pain! May the Forsaken behold him so renewed, and tremble! May their hearts quail with his screams of agony! And then shall the Pure descend, in a glorious blitzkrieg of Urfarah\u2019s justice!&gt;<br /> <br /> <i>The three </i>Anshega <i>then threw their heads to the sky and howled, the congregation immediately following suit, their voices melding together into a single, heart-stopping chorus. Suddenly, Tank\u2019s argent spirit brands flared to life, and then there was a white flash of teeth \u2013 a grin of pure sadistic glee \u2013 and the unsheathing of a single </i>Gauru<i>-sized claw. \u201cGood,\u201d said the speaker, Silent-Scream-the-Lambs, before plunging his claw into the blazing rune on the Forsaken warrior\u2019s forehead.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Tank screamed.</i><br /> <br /> -------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Purge the Impure</b><br /> <br /> An obscure, profane rite that transforms one of the Forsaken into a suicidal, pain-mad berserker, a living weapon forged for the sole purpose of slaying other Uratha. Three Anshega shamans \u2013 one for each of the three Pure tribes \u2013 must work in concert to perform the rite, and the target must be a werewolf who, at the very least, retains the spirit brands of Renown. Needless to say, this target - victim, really - must be kept immobilized throughout the entire ordeal. The power of the rite afflicts the victim with Silver Wolf\u2019s Agony, twisting his Renown brands into glyphs of blasphemy against Mother Luna which all bleed molten silver. It also fills him with Dire Wolf\u2019s Fury, causing him to change into a grotesque, albeit terrifyingly powerful, mockery of the Gauru. Lastly, the rite gives the victim Rabid Wolf\u2019s Fever, which causes him to burn like a raging inferno from within. This rite, in the rare occasions it is used, serves as the precursor to a pogrom that the Pure are about to unleash.<br /> <br /> Mechanically speaking, all the victim\u2019s close combat Brawl attacks inflict aggravated damage, and Uratha who inflict at least 1L upon him with a close combat Brawl attack suffers 1A from a splash of boiling-hot silver. The victim is also in a permanent state of Basu-Im - focused on chasing down and killing other werewolves - while taking on a horribly malformed shape commensurate in power to Primal Form. Lastly, the haze of incredible heat and outward pressure emanating from the victim\u2019s body imposes a -1 penalty to all close combat Brawl and Weaponry attacks made against him. More importantly, the victim explodes upon death or the rising of the sun, whichever comes first, instantly killing him (if he were not dead already) as well as inflicting 4 dice + 4 levels of lethal damage (aggravated for werewolves) to everything within 5 yards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3702,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","user":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","date":". 11-17-2014, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T11:00:16-08:00","id":314682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ursufgutha Storm-Born</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/310448-silver-madness-and-antagonists-in-armor?p=314586#post314586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Purge the Impure</b><br /> <br /> An obscure, profane rite that transforms one of the Forsaken into a suicidal, pain-mad berserker, a living weapon forged for the sole purpose of slaying other Uratha. Three Anshega shamans \u2013 one for each of the three Pure tribes \u2013 must work in concert to perform the rite, and the target must be a werewolf who, at the very least, retains the spirit brands of Renown. Needless to say, this target - victim, really - must be kept immobilized throughout the entire ordeal. The power of the rite afflicts the victim with Silver Wolf\u2019s Agony, twisting his Renown brands into glyphs of blasphemy against Mother Luna which all bleed molten silver. It also fills him with Dire Wolf\u2019s Fury, causing him to change into a grotesque, albeit terrifyingly powerful, mockery of the Gauru. Lastly, the rite gives the victim Rabid Wolf\u2019s Fever, which causes him to burn like a raging inferno from within. This rite, in the rare occasions it is used, serves as the precursor to a pogrom that the Pure are about to unleash.<br /> <br /> Mechanically speaking, all the victim\u2019s close combat Brawl attacks inflict aggravated damage, and Uratha who inflict at least 1L upon him with a close combat Brawl attack suffers 1A from a splash of boiling-hot silver. The victim is also in a permanent state of Basu-Im - focused on chasing down and killing other werewolves - while taking on a horribly malformed shape commensurate in power to Primal Form. Lastly, the haze of incredible heat and outward pressure emanating from the victim\u2019s body imposes a -1 penalty to all close combat Brawl and Weaponry attacks made against him. More importantly, the victim explodes upon death or the rising of the sun, whichever comes first, instantly killing him (if he were not dead already) as well as inflicting 4 dice + 4 levels of lethal damage (aggravated for werewolves) to everything within 5 yards.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty badass. I love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}